  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 723.08 Non-Central Treatment Device Monitoring Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 723.08 Non-Central Treatment Device Monitoring Requirements.\n\n(a) Unless otherwise specified in the treatment approval, the PWS owner shall collect a sample of treated water and have the sample tested for the contaminant(s) from each non-central treatment device:\n\n(1) Within 90 days of initial installation; and\n\n(2) Annually thereafter as specified in the PWS’s sampling schedule provided by the department in accordance with Env-Dw 708.\n\n(b) If any result from any non-central treatment device exceeds the MCL for the contaminant being treated, the PWS owner shall submit flow and maintenance records and results from all non-central treatment devices installed at that PWS to the department to collaboratively determine the frequency of subsequent monitoring of that device.\n\n(c) Compliance shall be determined for each device based on the running annual average of results from samples collected at each non-central treatment device.\n\nSource. #10618, eff 6-1-14, EXPIRED 6-1-24\n\nNew. #14119, eff 11-23-24, EXPIRES: 11-23-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
